#NEXUS
[Cladogram: synthetic example for demonstration only, NOT a biological inference.
 All taxa and relationships are fictional.
 Shared synthetic taxa: OTU01 through OTU15; shared strictly binary topology.
 Support values (prob) are fictional numbers for display only, not analysis results.
 Missing node prob values are filled with random synthetic values in [0.71, 1],
 for display testing only, NOT analysis results; existing values are preserved.
 No node ages, time anchors, or branch lengths are supplied.
 The rooted topology expresses relationships only, not elapsed time.]
BEGIN TREES;
  TREE fictional_cladogram = [&R]
    ((OTU01[&prob=0.914],OTU02[&prob=0.789])[&prob=0.96],
     (((OTU03[&prob=0.876],OTU04[&prob=0.804])[&prob=1.000],(OTU05[&prob=0.781],OTU06[&prob=0.810])[&prob=0.712])[&prob=0.973],
      (((OTU07[&prob=0.923],OTU08[&prob=0.809])[&prob=0.940],(OTU09[&prob=0.728],OTU10[&prob=0.927])[&prob=0.714])[&prob=0.963],
       ((OTU11[&prob=0.806],OTU12[&prob=0.747])[&prob=0.844],(OTU13[&prob=0.736],(OTU14[&prob=0.758],OTU15[&prob=0.910])[&prob=0.814])[&prob=0.809])[&prob=0.994])[&prob=0.889])[&prob=0.92])[&prob=0.891];
END;
